WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.568 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So "Wine Country."
I'm so excited.

00:00:01.568 --> 00:00:02.369 line:92%
I'm going to go to the premiere.

00:00:02.369 --> 00:00:03.603 align:start size:94% position:6%
All you guys are in town
on Wednesday.

00:00:03.603 --> 00:00:04.504 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-These are --

00:00:04.504 --> 00:00:06.172 align:start size:94% position:6%
These are
our dream team friends.

00:00:06.172 --> 00:00:06.606 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:00:06.606 --> 00:00:09.542 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's you, Poehler, Dratch,
Maya Rudolph.

00:00:09.542 --> 00:00:11.711 align:start size:94% position:6%
Tina's in the film.
-Emily Spivey and --

00:00:11.711 --> 00:00:14.547
-Emily Spivey and Liz Cackowski
wrote it.

00:00:14.547 --> 00:00:15.515 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And Paula Pell...
-And Paula Pell.

00:00:15.515 --> 00:00:16.349 line:92%
-...who's going to be, at 56,

00:00:16.349 --> 00:00:18.485 size:81% position:41%
the greatest discovery
ever to come to film.

00:00:18.485 --> 00:00:20.820 align:start size:94% position:6%
-A comedy gold mine.
-It's a powerhouse. Yes.

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:23.556 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And this is actually --
this film is based

00:00:23.556 --> 00:00:25.325
on an actual birthday weekend...
-Yes.

00:00:25.325 --> 00:00:27.494 size:78% position:39%
-...you guys all took
for Rachel Dratch.

00:00:27.494 --> 00:00:28.094 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-That's right.

00:00:28.094 --> 00:00:32.098 size:75% position:38%
We celebrate marquee
birthdays together.

00:00:32.098 --> 00:00:34.034 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yep.
-And we did go to Sonoma

00:00:34.034 --> 00:00:35.035 line:92%
to celebrate Dratch's birthday.

00:00:35.035 --> 00:00:37.504 size:88% position:44%
And a lot of the sort of
tentpoles of the movie

00:00:37.504 --> 00:00:40.573 align:start size:94% position:6%
are based on real moments
that we spent for Dratch's --

00:00:40.573 --> 00:00:42.142 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we also did it
for my birthday.

00:00:42.142 --> 00:00:44.644 align:start size:94% position:6%
Two years ago,
we went to Palm Springs.

00:00:44.644 --> 00:00:45.311 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-And what do you guys --

00:00:45.311 --> 00:00:47.414
what does this group of women
that everyone knows so well --

00:00:47.414 --> 00:00:49.416 align:start size:94% position:6%
what do you do
on a birthday weekend?

00:00:49.416 --> 00:00:50.617 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We pick a theme.
-Uh-huh.

00:00:50.617 --> 00:00:51.918 line:92%
-I mean, again, you would think

00:00:51.918 --> 00:00:54.421 align:start size:94% position:6%
that that would mean
like greasers or something.

00:00:54.421 --> 00:00:55.488 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Light laughter ]
No, for mine,

00:00:55.488 --> 00:00:59.592
I really wanted to wear muumuus
the whole time.

00:00:59.592 --> 00:01:00.727 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Uh-huh.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:00.727 --> 00:01:03.363 align:start size:94% position:6%
And -- And I bought everybody
vintage bathing caps.

00:01:03.363 --> 00:01:05.598 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
And then...

00:01:05.598 --> 00:01:06.366 size:81% position:41% line:92%
And we were in a phase

00:01:06.366 --> 00:01:08.134 align:start size:94% position:6%
where we were really enjoying
bitching about things.

00:01:08.134 --> 00:01:10.003 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay.
-And so Spivey named it

00:01:10.003 --> 00:01:11.371 align:start size:94% position:6%
the "Muumuu Nitpick."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:11.371 --> 00:01:14.107 size:88% position:44%
And then, we just, like,
floated around in a pool

00:01:14.107 --> 00:01:15.775 align:start size:94% position:6%
and complained about stuff
you can't say a lot.

00:01:15.775 --> 00:01:17.177 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like the parts you didn't like
in "Hamilton" --

00:01:17.177 --> 00:01:18.478 align:start size:94% position:6%
like, stuff like that.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:18.478 --> 00:01:19.312 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.
-You know --

00:01:19.312 --> 00:01:21.414
like, things you can't say in
front of a lot of other people.

00:01:21.414 --> 00:01:22.482 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, of course, right.
-So we just --

00:01:22.482 --> 00:01:23.550 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, it's very --
you want to be, like,

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:25.151
safely in the center of a pool.
-You just want to --

00:01:25.151 --> 00:01:26.920 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean you want to let it fly,
you know?

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:27.854 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-With some of the things

00:01:27.854 --> 00:01:29.556 align:start size:94% position:6%
that aren't so fashionable
to say.

00:01:29.556 --> 00:01:32.192
-And this is a photo
of some of you guys hanging out.

00:01:32.192 --> 00:01:33.259 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, that's
a good time picture.

00:01:33.259 --> 00:01:35.161 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's a good time.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:35.161 --> 00:01:37.263 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's my favorite picture
of all time, actually,

00:01:37.263 --> 00:01:40.467
because that's a bunch of idiots
who just had rosé at lunch

00:01:40.467 --> 00:01:42.001 align:start size:94% position:6%
is what that is.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:42.001 --> 00:01:44.104 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This is a cake
that was made for you.

00:01:44.104 --> 00:01:45.138 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, yeah, okay,
so, let me explain.

00:01:45.138 --> 00:01:46.372
-Okay, yeah, yeah. Here.
-Let me explain. Let me explain.

00:01:46.372 --> 00:01:48.174
Reveal. We got to --
I'm sorry -- I didn't mean to --

00:01:48.174 --> 00:01:48.842 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-No, no, please, please.

00:01:48.842 --> 00:01:50.810 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I didn't mean to -- to harsh
your -- your reveal.

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:54.047 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Light laughter ]
So, for our cakes, what we do,

00:01:54.047 --> 00:01:54.781 size:88% position:44% line:92%
which makes us laugh is,

00:01:54.781 --> 00:01:57.650 align:start size:94% position:6%
we celebrate a character
that maybe wasn't as beloved.

00:01:57.650 --> 00:01:58.518 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Sure.
-Because you know,

00:01:58.518 --> 00:01:59.786 size:81% position:41%
as people on the show,
your favorite moments

00:01:59.786 --> 00:02:02.355
are either funny things that
happened in the writer's room...

00:02:02.355 --> 00:02:03.356 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-...or in rehearsal.

00:02:03.356 --> 00:02:05.959
They're generally not the things
that everybody else enjoys.

00:02:05.959 --> 00:02:07.193 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.
-So I -- I had

00:02:07.193 --> 00:02:10.997
this character Deandra Wells,
who was moderately popular.

00:02:10.997 --> 00:02:13.032 align:start size:94% position:6%
For -- For Dratch's birthday,
we did Abe Scheinwald.

00:02:13.032 --> 00:02:13.900 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yep.
-The accountant --

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:15.502 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean the --
-Yep, double D's, double D's.

00:02:15.502 --> 00:02:16.769 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Movie producer --
double D's, double D's.

00:02:16.769 --> 00:02:17.770 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yep.
-And we featured a cake

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:20.039 align:start size:94% position:6%
with flowers and a lot
of $20 and $50 dollar bills

00:02:20.039 --> 00:02:21.341 align:start size:94% position:6%
coming out of it.
[ Light laughter ]

00:02:21.341 --> 00:02:23.610 size:84% position:42%
You can look at the --
look at the recognition

00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:24.777 align:start size:94% position:6%
for Abe Scheinwald.
-Yeah.

00:02:24.777 --> 00:02:26.212 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-It was extraordinary.

00:02:26.212 --> 00:02:27.981 align:start size:94% position:6%
You can Google it, so...
-You can Google it.

00:02:27.981 --> 00:02:28.715 size:75% position:38% line:92%
It's worth a Google.

00:02:28.715 --> 00:02:30.183 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's worth a real
satisfying Google.

00:02:30.183 --> 00:02:31.384 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And yours truly wrote it.

00:02:31.384 --> 00:02:32.385 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And don't worry
you're gonna, like,

00:02:32.385 --> 00:02:34.888
lose hours and hours watching
them -- there's only like two.

00:02:34.888 --> 00:02:35.922 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:35.922 --> 00:02:37.724 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, this was true
also of my sketch.

00:02:37.724 --> 00:02:39.092 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. Yeah.
-Deandra Wells,

00:02:39.092 --> 00:02:41.995 line:92%
who was a real -- a real [bleep]

00:02:41.995 --> 00:02:43.496 align:start size:94% position:6%
Am I allowed to say that?
-Yeah, yeah.

00:02:43.496 --> 00:02:44.998 align:start size:94% position:6%
-She --
She was a singer, very --

00:02:44.998 --> 00:02:48.234
talked about love all the time,
but very abusive to her band.

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:50.870 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, hello, band.
Nice to see you guys.

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:52.071 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:52.071 --> 00:02:54.240 align:start size:94% position:6%
So we -- she --
she had -- she --

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:55.475 line:92%
We had one with Conan O'Brien,

00:02:55.475 --> 00:02:56.676 align:start size:94% position:6%
where she was real abusive
to him

00:02:56.676 --> 00:02:58.011 align:start size:94% position:6%
while he was
coming out of rehab.

00:02:58.011 --> 00:03:01.548 align:start size:94% position:6%
He was her son.
And it was set --

00:03:01.548 --> 00:03:04.217
And for some reason, it was her
"Live in Santa Barbara" concert.

00:03:04.217 --> 00:03:06.653
And for some reason,
when he finally explodes at her,

00:03:06.653 --> 00:03:08.421
she turns to everybody --
the character -- and says,

00:03:08.421 --> 00:03:11.024 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Not here,
not in Santa Barbara!"

00:03:11.024 --> 00:03:12.091 size:81% position:41% line:92%
as though it mattered.

00:03:12.091 --> 00:03:13.660 align:start size:94% position:6%
Santa Barbara had nothing
to do with it.

00:03:13.660 --> 00:03:14.561 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.
-So on my cake,

00:03:14.561 --> 00:03:16.529 align:start size:94% position:6%
they did a giant blowup
of Deandra Wells.

00:03:16.529 --> 00:03:17.897 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she did have icing
that said,

00:03:17.897 --> 00:03:19.799 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Not here,
not in Santa Barbara!"

00:03:19.799 --> 00:03:20.967 align:start size:94% position:6%
and with exploding candles,
so...

00:03:20.967 --> 00:03:24.871 size:84% position:42%
[ Cheers and Applause ]
-But now, this is --

00:03:24.871 --> 00:03:26.206 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-So much detail.

00:03:26.206 --> 00:03:28.041 align:start size:94% position:6%
Again, I would say...
-But not in --

00:03:28.041 --> 00:03:29.042 line:92%
-...I would say Google it.

00:03:29.042 --> 00:03:30.310 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm sure
it's not on the Internet,

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:32.378 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause NBC doesn't want to pay
for the music rights.

00:03:32.378 --> 00:03:33.046 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-So...

00:03:33.046 --> 00:03:35.348
An, once again,
band, can I get a, "What what?"

00:03:35.348 --> 00:03:37.083 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I was -- this was
very familiar to me,

00:03:37.083 --> 00:03:38.618 align:start size:94% position:6%
because when I started
on the show...

00:03:38.618 --> 00:03:40.386 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-...in your office...

00:03:40.386 --> 00:03:40.820 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:42.722
-...you had a giant oil painting
of Deandra.

00:03:42.722 --> 00:03:44.557 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, it was huge.
It's absolutely huge.

00:03:44.557 --> 00:03:46.025 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-I mean, I'm not kidding.

00:03:46.025 --> 00:03:48.161 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think it's 4 by 11 feet.
It's massive.

00:03:48.161 --> 00:03:51.431
Because it was a sketch that
we took to dress and was cut.

00:03:51.431 --> 00:03:54.534 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was --
It was cut because it bombed.

00:03:54.534 --> 00:03:55.368 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Pretty badly.

00:03:55.368 --> 00:03:57.804 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was a -- It was a short --
a play --

00:03:57.804 --> 00:03:59.872 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Yeah.
-A one-act play.

00:03:59.872 --> 00:04:00.807 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And was it one of those
sketches

00:04:00.807 --> 00:04:02.442 align:start size:94% position:6%
where you --
very early on, you knew,

00:04:02.442 --> 00:04:04.277
"Oh, this is bombing, and we're
not gonna get it back?"

00:04:04.277 --> 00:04:06.145 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, it was a --
it was a Christmas special.

00:04:06.145 --> 00:04:07.947 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we got real lost
in the details.

00:04:07.947 --> 00:04:09.148 align:start size:94% position:6%
Paula and I wrote it together.
-Yeah.

00:04:09.148 --> 00:04:10.049 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-And we got real excited

00:04:10.049 --> 00:04:12.785
about this giant self-portrait,
for example,

00:04:12.785 --> 00:04:14.087 line:92%
that she would have in her home.

00:04:14.087 --> 00:04:15.321 line:92%
She had -- It was a Christmas --

00:04:15.321 --> 00:04:16.289 align:start size:94% position:6%
like a Christmas
variety special.

00:04:16.289 --> 00:04:20.159
And she had -- And Val Kilmer
was playing Kris Kristofferson.

00:04:20.159 --> 00:04:21.160 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:24.264 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we had individual
jewel cases of CD covers

00:04:24.264 --> 00:04:24.931 line:92%
all over her Christmas --

00:04:24.931 --> 00:04:27.200 align:start size:94% position:6%
We really -- We really
brought it in on the details.

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:29.168
But we forgot to write comedy...
-Right.

00:04:29.168 --> 00:04:30.336 align:start size:94% position:6%
-...is the problem.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:30.336 --> 00:04:32.872 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so, it was a play
about a woman

00:04:32.872 --> 00:04:34.841 align:start size:94% position:6%
who had a Christmas special
that was bad.

00:04:34.841 --> 00:04:35.808 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, I remember...
-Yeah.

00:04:35.808 --> 00:04:37.277 align:start size:94% position:6%
-...it was, literally,
Big Bird came --

00:04:37.277 --> 00:04:40.013 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it was --
and -- and small children.

00:04:40.013 --> 00:04:40.880 align:start size:94% position:6%
It wasn't funny.
-And --

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:42.815 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But, anyway, so...
[ Laughter ]

00:04:42.815 --> 00:04:46.286 line:92%
...this portrait -- the --

00:04:46.286 --> 00:04:47.320 align:start size:94% position:6%
Joe DeTullio...
-Yeah.

00:04:47.320 --> 00:04:49.022 align:start size:94% position:6%
-...said to me, "Hey,
we got this giant portrait.

00:04:49.022 --> 00:04:51.524 align:start size:94% position:6%
You want it in your office?"
Of course I said yes.

00:04:51.524 --> 00:04:53.092 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because my office was...
-Yeah.

00:04:53.092 --> 00:04:56.896
-...you know, about --
I don't know -- 10 square feet.

00:04:56.896 --> 00:04:58.364 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so it took up
a lot of real estate.

00:04:58.364 --> 00:04:59.132 line:92%
-It took up all the space.

00:04:59.132 --> 00:05:00.233 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It took up a lot
of real estate.

00:05:00.233 --> 00:05:01.367 line:92%
And then, when I left the show,

00:05:01.367 --> 00:05:03.202 align:start size:94% position:6%
I guess it hung around
the writers' room for a while?

00:05:03.202 --> 00:05:05.004 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was there a long time.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:05.004 --> 00:05:06.039 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was --
It was my way of saying,

00:05:06.039 --> 00:05:08.608 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I'm still here, friends."
-[ Laughing ] Yeah.

00:05:08.608 --> 00:05:10.677 align:start size:94% position:6%
The eyes followed you
when you walk across the room.

00:05:10.677 --> 00:05:12.178 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, ex--
[ Laughter ]

00:05:12.178 --> 00:05:14.547 line:92%
So I ran into Andrew Steele --

00:05:14.547 --> 00:05:15.648 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know --
a few years later.

00:05:15.648 --> 00:05:17.050 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's like I can see
that portrait every day.

00:05:17.050 --> 00:05:18.985
You might -- You might think
about getting that at home.

00:05:18.985 --> 00:05:20.520 align:start size:94% position:6%
And weirdly,
I don't have any pictures

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:21.621 align:start size:94% position:6%
from "Saturday Night Live"
in my house.

00:05:21.621 --> 00:05:24.691 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, strangely,
my husband really wanted this.

00:05:24.691 --> 00:05:28.795
And so it hangs in my front hall
to this day.

00:05:28.795 --> 00:05:29.462 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And it's fantastic,

00:05:29.462 --> 00:05:31.564 size:84% position:42%
'cause there are people
who come into my home

00:05:31.564 --> 00:05:32.832 align:start size:94% position:6%
who think
we had this commissioned.

00:05:32.832 --> 00:05:34.600 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
You know what I mean?

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:35.134 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:05:35.134 --> 00:05:36.469 align:start size:94% position:6%
'Cause it's not
a famous character.

00:05:36.469 --> 00:05:37.470 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No.
-So they walk in,

00:05:37.470 --> 00:05:40.006 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they're like,
"What -- So, did Charlie --

00:05:40.006 --> 00:05:41.474 size:88% position:44% line:92%
Was it your 40th or...?"

00:05:41.474 --> 00:05:42.442 size:84% position:42% line:92%
You know, they think --

00:05:42.442 --> 00:05:45.244
You know,
it's like a Mar-a-Lago painting.

00:05:45.244 --> 00:05:46.012 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It is.
-You know?

00:05:46.012 --> 00:05:47.447 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter and applause ]
It's full Mar-a-Lago.

00:05:47.447 --> 00:05:48.981
-Yeah.
I've got some Mar-a-Lago vibes.

00:05:48.981 --> 00:05:50.783 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This is a nice --
this is a true story, though,

00:05:50.783 --> 00:05:53.519 size:88% position:44%
because you do have more
in common with Deandra

00:05:53.519 --> 00:05:54.253 size:84% position:42% line:92%
than you're letting on.

00:05:54.253 --> 00:05:56.756
You actually do have a Christmas
album coming out this year...

00:05:56.756 --> 00:05:57.623 align:start size:94% position:6%
